# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the clang-asan test presets (CMakePresets.json sets
# LSAN_OPTIONS). Only reports from inside a third-party library belong here, each with
# its reason; a leak through put.gd code is fixed, not suppressed (#2065).
#
# Ubuntu 26.04's fontconfig (2.17) leaks the configuration state it parses with expat
# the first time Qt adds an application font: QFontDatabase::addApplicationFont ->
# QFontconfigDatabase::addApplicationFont -> FcConfigGetFonts -> XML_ParseBuffer.
# 320 bytes once per process, in every test that loads put.gd's bundled fonts
# (src/ui/Fonts.cpp), and in the helpers they start, which then exit non-zero.
# Fedora 45's fontconfig doesn't. A `leak:` rule matches any frame of the allocation
# stack, and fontconfig never calls back into put.gd, so this can't hide a put.gd leak.
leak:FcConfigGetFonts
